<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Nothing, and the emptiness is the point — the same argument the Mac's
	     Spektrafilm.entitlements makes, for the same reason.

	     Everything this app reads arrives through the document picker or a
	     drag from Files, which hands out security-scoped URLs
	     (`SecurityScopedURLs` in PadLibrary.swift holds them for the life of
	     the process). Nothing here needs iCloud, push, App Groups, HealthKit
	     or any of the other capabilities that would turn this file into a list
	     of holes in the sandbox.

	     One entitlement is deliberately *not* written: `com.apple.developer
	     .team-identifier` and the associated-domains family are provisioning
	     concerns, and a signature that needs them is a distribution decision,
	     not a port decision. Debug and development builds sign with the
	     automatic profile and `get-task-allow` is added by the toolchain. -->
</dict>
</plist>
